7.2 Verification Protocol

A design is accepted only if:

1. All constraints satisfied by primary models (Agents A–E, I);
2. Primary and verification models agree within tolerance;
3. Design lies on the Pareto front of the current population;
4. Rotordynamic stability margin satisfied.

Passing designs are labeled "computationally consistent candidate." They are not labeled "validated."

