15. Closing Statement

This project investigates a narrow, falsifiable question: does LLM-generated architectural prior improve the sample efficiency of physics-constrained design-space exploration, under a fixed verification budget, at equivalent repair and cost?

The answer may be yes. The answer may be no. Either outcome is a scientific result.

The framework is built from conservation laws, port-typed graph grammars, validated component models, independent verification, explicit uncertainty, and reproducible computation. The LLM is a proposal generator, not an oracle. The equations decide what survives.

