Appendix D: Peng–Robinson Equation of State and Departure Functions

D.1 Generalized Peng–Robinson EOS

The generalized Peng–Robinson equation of state is:

P = \frac{RT}{V - b} - \frac{a(T)}{V(V+b) + b(V-b)}

with:

b = 0.07780 \frac{R T_c}{P_c}

a(T) = a(T_c) \alpha(T) = 0.45724 \frac{R^2 T_c^2}{P_c} \alpha(T)

\sqrt{\alpha} = 1 + \kappa\left(1 - \sqrt{T/T_c}\right)

\kappa = 0.37464 + 1.54226\omega - 0.26992\omega^2

where  \omega  is the acentric factor.

D.2 Compressibility Factor

The compressibility factor  Z = PV/(RT)  satisfies the cubic equation:

Z^3 + \alpha Z^2 + \beta Z + \gamma = 0

where:

\alpha = -1 + B

\beta = A - 3B^2 - 2B

\gamma = -AB + B^2 + B^3

A = \frac{aP}{R^2 T^2}, \quad B = \frac{bP}{RT}

D.3 Enthalpy Departure Function

The enthalpy departure function from ideal-gas behavior is:

h - h^{\text{ig}} = RT(Z - 1) + \frac{T\frac{da}{dT} - a}{2\sqrt{2}b}\ln\left[\frac{Z + (1+\sqrt{2})B}{Z + (1-\sqrt{2})B}\right]

D.4 Entropy Departure Function

The entropy departure function is:

s - s^{\text{ig}} = R\ln(Z - B) + \frac{1}{2\sqrt{2}b}\frac{da}{dT}\ln\left[\frac{Z + (1+\sqrt{2})B}{Z + (1-\sqrt{2})B}\right]

D.5 Derivative of Attraction Parameter

\frac{da}{dT} = 0.45724 \frac{R^2 T_c^2}{P_c} \frac{d\alpha}{dT}

\frac{d\alpha}{dT} = -\frac{\kappa}{\sqrt{T T_c}} \left(1 + \kappa\left(1 - \sqrt{T/T_c}\right)\right)

