Appendix I: Groeneveld CHF Table — Extrapolation Analysis

I.1 Table Derivation

The 2006 CHF look-up table is a normalized data bank for a vertical 8 mm water-cooled tube, based on a database containing more than 30,000 data points, providing CHF values at 24 pressures, 20 mass fluxes, and 23 qualities. The table covers water over a wide range of conditions.

I.2 Extrapolation to Cryogenic Propellants

Application to cryogenic propellants (LN₂, LCH₄, LOX) in additively manufactured cooling channels is an extrapolation with unknown error. The table was derived for water in nuclear channels; cryogenic fluids have different surface tension, latent heat, and wetting characteristics.

V0.4 uncertainty treatment. Constraint 8 is labeled [ASSUMED-EXTRAPOLATED] with a factor-of-2 uncertainty band on  q''_{\text{CHF}} . Designs with  q''_{\text{local}} > 0.5 q''_{\text{CHF}}  are flagged for sensitivity analysis.

I.3 Correction Factors

The Groeneveld 1986 CHF chart method is standardized for 8 mm circular tubes and provides correction factors for various channel geometries. These correction factors must be extended to cryogenic conditions with additional uncertainty.

